   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1f16a5c3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# KDD Process Project\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements the **Knowledge Discovery in Databases (KDD)** process.  We focus on selection, preprocessing, transformation, data mining and interpretation using the credit card fraud dataset.  Unlike the previous methodologies, here we experiment with an unsupervised anomaly detection algorithm."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4bc53e34",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Selection & Preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "All records are retained to train the unsupervised model.  Features are standardised to zero mean and unit variance.  No class labels are used during training.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Expert Review & Recommendations\n",
    "In anomaly detection, retaining as much normal behaviour as possible helps the model learn what ‘normal’ looks like.  Care must be taken not to leak label information."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7f6de682",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "# Load the data\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('../dataset/creditcard.csv')\n",
    "X = df.drop(columns=['Class'])\n",
    "y = df['Class']\n",
    "# Standardise features\n",
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X)\n",
    "# For unsupervised anomaly detection, we keep all data (no train/test split)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "98565758",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Transformation, Data Mining & Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "We train an Isolation Forest to learn the ‘normal’ pattern of credit card transactions.  It assigns anomaly scores; points with scores below a threshold are labelled as potential fraud.  Mapping these predictions back to the known labels allows us to evaluate how well the unsupervised approach performs.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Expert Review & Recommendations\n",
    "Isolation Forest offers a quick baseline.  More sophisticated methods like autoencoders or one‑class SVMs could improve performance.  In practice, unsupervised methods are valuable when labels are scarce or unreliable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b788d859",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Train an Isolation Forest to detect anomalies\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import IsolationForest\n",
    "iso = IsolationForest(n_estimators=100, contamination=0.001, random_state=42)\n",
    "iso.fit(X_scaled)\n",
    "# Predict anomalies (-1 for outliers, 1 for inliers)\n",
    "scores = iso.decision_function(X_scaled)\n",
    "y_pred = iso.predict(X_scaled)\n",
    "# Map predictions to fraud (1) or not (0) where -1 is anomaly\n",
    "y_pred_labels = np.where(y_pred == -1, 1, 0)\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import confusion_matrix, precision_score, recall_score, f1_score\n",
    "cm = confusion_matrix(y, y_pred_labels)\n",
    "prec = precision_score(y, y_pred_labels)\n",
    "rec = recall_score(y, y_pred_labels)\n",
    "f1 = f1_score(y, y_pred_labels)\n",
    "print('Confusion matrix:', cm)\n",
    "print(f'Precision: {prec:.4f}, Recall: {rec:.4f}, F1: {f1:.4f}')"
   ]
  }
 ],
